WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
Now, I hope you have been saving words
and learning these words, or at least

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.179
reviewing them. Don't worry if you
remember them, you're gonna forget them.

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:15.480
But now you should try to save phrases,
because very often the individual words

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:21.029
don't give you a good sense of what the
words mean together in a phrase. If you

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:24.930
save the phrase, you'll hear the
text-to-speech, you'll get a translation,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:30.359
which may or may not always be accurate,
but I find mostly it is, and then you

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:35.460
want to review these phrases, because
phrases have the advantage that that

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.600
they help you prepare to speak, because
when you go to speak you want to use

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.460
words that kind of belong together, that
are normally used together. So you should

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.170
get used to these. Direct your attention
to these phrases by saving them. You will

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.910
notice that other users have saved
phrases, and you'll see these sort of

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:58.320
outlined for you, suggested as example
phrases that you could save. Where

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.600
possible, save phrases and review them.
It'll be a big boost to your language

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.979
learning. Good luck!

